{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/658685-the-doggy-dictionary","id":658685,"title":"The Doggy Dictionary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T17:41:22-07:00","id":658685,"title":"The Doggy Dictionary","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">So in a world without humans, where animals are hyper evolved, obviously the dialect is going to change some for the residents of Pugmire. The purpose of this thread is a bit of fun for us to pose ideas for what we think certain words could / would mean in a world governed by dogs.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alpha:</b> A social, political or militaristic leader. The one in charge of a particular group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Heel:</b> Come closer, follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Puppy:</b> Child, underage dog. (alternatively 'pup')<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Puppies:</b> Plural term for puppy. (alternatively 'pups')<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Relic:</b> Artifacts of Man left behind after their extinction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Man:</b> The collective human race. (alternatively, a male human)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Code of Man:</b> The predominate religion / philosophy that dogs strive to adhere to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Good Dog:</b> A dog who dutifully lives by the Code of Man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bad Dog:</b> A dog who violates or refuses to live by the Code of Man<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bitch:</b> A female canine of any breed. Unlike in the time of Man, the word is not considered insulting to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rabid:</b> A state of criminally dangerous and presumably incurable mental instability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hound:</b> A soldier<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shepherd:</b> A law enforcement agent<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Neuter:</b> The act of castration, particularly upon males.While normally reserved for punishing Bad Dogs, some radicals believe voluntary neutering is a sign of one's devotion to the Code of Man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pound, the:</b> A correctional facility. A prison or jailhouse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Muzzle:</b> A restraining device used to prevent Bad Dogs from using their fangs on others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Leash:</b> A restraining device used to forcefully escort Bad Dogs from one destination to another, as well as keep them from running away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2015, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:55:05-07:00","id":660758,"title":"","content":"<b>Lap Dog:</b> A sycophant, a mooch. An adult dog who relies on others to provide for their well being.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rat Dog:</b> A dog who is prone to making empty threats. A racial slur for breeds of diminutive size.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Obedience School:</b> An educational facility where one can receive training in the Code of Man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Collar:</b> A restraining device used to denote one's status as a prisoner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bath, a:</b> A form of torture involving repeatedly submersing the victim in water.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fetch:</b> To retrieve something for someone. To return lost or stolen property to its rightful owner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tummy Rub:</b> A frontal massage particularly focusing on the abdominal region..<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:32:28-07:00","id":667354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/658685-the-doggy-dictionary#post658685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hound:</b> A soldier or law enforcement agent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a thought: Why not:<br /> <br /> <b>Hound:</b> A soldier.<br /> <br /> <b>Shepherd:</b> A law enforcement agent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:56:38-07:00","id":667472,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, that does make more sense. Leading the flock, kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T18:53:10-07:00","id":667717,"title":"","content":"<b>Sniff</b><b>:</b> Slang synonym for &quot;investigate&quot; - can be used as a verb or noun (e.g. &quot;We took a sniff.&quot;). This is in addition to its normal meaning, &quot;to smell&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Lick: </b>To show affection. (e.g. &quot;What kind of bitch never licks her pups?&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Wag: </b>A physical sign of happiness/satisfaction. (e.g. &quot;Whatever he says, just keep wagging until he goes away.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Housebroken</b>: Civilized, cultured, clean. (e.g. &quot;Look at how he grooms himself - now that's a housebroken dog!&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf: </b>Barbarian, unhousebroken dog. Sometimes used in reference to Bad Dogs to denote aggressive behavior.<br /> <br /> <b>Fox: </b>Bad Dog who lies or steals regularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:56:40-07:00","id":668182,"title":"","content":"It's awesome that you folks are discussing this! It looks like a lot of interesting ideas. I did want to mention quickly, however, that the word &quot;bitch&quot; won't be used in Pugmire -- while there was at one point a valid canine use of the word, it doesn't add enough value to the game to overcome the connotations we have placed on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:35:34-07:00","id":668234,"title":"","content":"Aww. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> btw, I tried to shy away from using other species (wolf / fox) as slang because it was stated they were thinking of ideas for other races. Didn't want to risk confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:18:29-07:00","id":668276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/658685-the-doggy-dictionary?p=668234#post668234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">btw, I tried to shy away from using other species (wolf / fox) as slang because it was stated they were thinking of ideas for other races. Didn't want to risk confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of that, but then it occured to me that Dogs are not necessarily immune to racist or speciest stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T06:52:11-07:00","id":669612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/658685-the-doggy-dictionary?p=667354#post667354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought: Why not:<br /> <br /> <b>Hound:</b> A soldier.<br /> <br /> <b>Shepherd:</b> A law enforcement agent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't shepherds <i>clergy</i>, like Picassa Collie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:42:15-07:00","id":670032,"title":"","content":"I was thinking in terms of, like, <i>German </i>Shepherd... but anyway, I think that the connotation of &quot;shepherding the flock&quot; being applied to the clergy would be a more human interpretation. If this is a society of uplifted dogs, I would think the flock-guarding tradition of many of the larger (built) sheep-herding breeds would be more prominent in their minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:29:27-07:00","id":670094,"title":"","content":"<b>Dog Catcher:</b> A restraining device once used by ancient humans in the shape of a pole with a spring locked collar on one end. It is used to capture bad dogs while keeping them at a safe distance.<br /> <br /> (Dog version of a Man Catcher, but less gruesome.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mutt:</b> A derogatory term for dogs of mixed breeding or poor upbringing. Primarily used by those of the upper class.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pedigree:</b> A term for dogs of strong lineages and pure bloodlines. Primarily used by those of the upper class.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Chew Toy:</b> A soft, durable material that is highly resistant to wear and tear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ball:</b> An orb, a spherical shaped object.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T17:41:04-07:00","id":690626,"title":"","content":"<b>Peta:</b> A blasphemous cult who claims beasts should forsake the Code of Man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Car Ride:</b> A tempting trap, an offer that seems too good to be true. (This sounds like a car ride, to me!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stray:</b> A homeless beast, a wanderer, a vagabond.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lassie:</b> A dog sent to retrieve emergency help. (If that Lassie hadn't been so fast, you might have drowned!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:03:16-07:00","id":691377,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Ankle-biter: </b></span><br /> A Dog that has gained notoriety through dueling. Usually describes lethal duelists from the less physically-imposing Families.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Note: Sometime used to describe fencers from other Houses, such as Pug and Terrier, it is more frequently used to describe the blademasters of House Chihuahua.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Yappy:</b></span><br /> To be an overtly vocal proponent of the Code of Man. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Scoot:</b></span><br /> The act of scratching an itch that develops in a nigh-unreachable part the body, one that cannot be scratched without the aid of an external structure such as a wall or floor.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T07:23:42-07:00","id":704951,"title":"","content":"<b>Vack-Oom:</b> A mythical creature said to relentlessly terrorize dogs in the time of man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T07:45:39-07:00","id":706841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/658685-the-doggy-dictionary?p=704951#post704951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vack-Oom:</b> A mythical creature said to relentlessly terrorize dogs in the time of man.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G4Sn91t1V4g\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;It can eat and yell at the same time. And I've seen it eat <i>everything</i>- seriously, like, a paperclip and <i>two </i>cat toys. Didn't even flinch.&quot;</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T14:19:59-08:00","id":770947,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer Shepard to be county farming dogs or clergy. Pugmire seems steeped in medieval analogs. Just because many people on this forum have a stigma against overt Christian references doesn't mean they have to be so PC as to avoid them. Hounds are trackers not soldiers so they come closer to law enforcement/bounty hunter/detective, &quot;Come on officer, stop hounding me&quot;<br /> <br /> Mastiffs are guards/soldier breeds by nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T15:09:10-08:00","id":770987,"title":"","content":"I thought I made shepherd a clergyman on my first draft. Must have changed it afterward and forgotten about it.<br /> <br /> But yeah, sheep dogs leading the flock sounds / sounded like an appropriate name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T22:19:31-08:00","id":799060,"title":"","content":"<b>Barker:</b> A town crier, an advertised spokesman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:58:35-08:00","id":818165,"title":"","content":"(Hey! First time posting in the Pugmire forums but I loved this idea so contributing a little.)<br /> <br /> The Weesperer - An angel or Saint figure. A Man who helped lead dogs closer to following the Code of Man.<br /> <br /> The Vet - A lost horror of the Age of Man, said to have been more terrifying than the Vack-Oom. Little is known of this fearful entity, other than that it terrified early dogs, and sometimes &quot;put them down&quot;.<br /> <br /> Pack - Group of friends/adopted family.<br /> <br /> Dog Park - colloquial term for safe or personal space. Analogous to &quot;Man Cave&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:40:27-08:00","id":819811,"title":"","content":"Blondi- A dog who is loyal to their master despite that master's wickedness. Legend claims the name dates back to a war between the gods, in which Blondi was a dog who served the leader of the wrong side.<br /> <br /> Brian- A dog who is smarter than their master, but serves them anyway because they fear that their master couldn't survive without them. Heretics claim the name comes from a comedic epic written by man in which a dog of the same name was more intelligent than most of the family of man that he served.<br /> <br /> Spaghetti Kiss- a term for a romantic encounter between two dogs of different social standing.<br /> <br /> Diz Nee- a great storyteller among man. several of his works center around dog kind, with his other works focusing on other species (particularly cats, foxes, ducks and mice, though almost every species was a subject of his works at some point) or on females born of man's nobility. His works are well known among educated dogs and most can quote extensively from them. Some dog scholars argue that some works attributed to him were actually written by others under his name after his death and the identity of the associate of Diz Nee known only as Pics Arr is a matter of great debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:54:39-08:00","id":820397,"title":"","content":"(Here goes nothing)<br /> <br /> Stud: a male of negotiable affections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:24:50-07:00","id":952869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/658685-the-doggy-dictionary?p=668182#post668182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's awesome that you folks are discussing this! It looks like a lot of interesting ideas. I did want to mention quickly, however, that the word &quot;bitch&quot; won't be used in Pugmire -- while there was at one point a valid canine use of the word, it doesn't add enough value to the game to overcome the connotations we have placed on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. I'm a total cat person but I'm totally interested in this game and happy such a derogatory term isn't being used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T15:47:42-08:00","id":1050121,"title":"","content":"<b>High-drant</b> - The equivalent of a proper indoor toilet, usually in the homes of wealthier dogs who can afford such luxuries, as opposed to more typical chamber pots or even just the field that the common dog might have. A cheaper public outhouse might even be called a<b> Low-drant</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13011-arran","name":"Arran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:09:30-07:00","id":1069751,"title":"","content":"A little glimpse of the future <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EWHaG_uCvEA\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T06:07:37-07:00","id":1070007,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, Rock and Rule! I had forgotten about that movie!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:41:27-07:00","id":1070892,"title":"","content":"<b>Tricks:</b> A professional set of skills or training. (You can't teach an old dog new tricks)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}